# eOn SVN r2549. HarnessCounter through ext_pot. Kernel lj_cut.
# L-BFGS memory 20 on the 1000 LJ38 starts at force sigma 1e-2. Settings match eon-svn/lbfgs-m20 except the potential: unshifted lj/cut, epsilon 1, sigma 1, cutoff 40, which is the problem potential, not lj_cluster. converged_force in this file is the clean tolerance 0.01. The run sets the client tolerance to max(0.01, 3 * sigma * sqrt(114)). When sigma is positive, a force sample under that threshold is held above it until the clean energy over the last 5 evaluations spans at most max(1e-10, 3 * sigma). The seed for start i is 20261016 + i. Success also requires a clean vibrational Hessian index of 0, with the six rigid modes removed. Energy and Kabsch RMSD are not applied: the problem file has no per-start reference. r2549 does not read energy_weighted, ci_mmf, climbing_image_band_slack, setup_mmf_peaks, or the develop L-BFGS catalog past memory, inverse curvature, max inverse curvature, auto scale, and the two resets. Those keys are omitted. The keys it does read sit in [Optimizer]. The binary is SVN r2549, the registry pin. Export of the 2014 revision is forbidden, so this row is r2549.
# Each start is the mean of 2 replicates (svn-all and fortran). n is the number of distinct starts. 0 starts differ in force_calls. Success agrees on every start.
counter harness
code Eon svn
code_version r2549
commit r2549
algorithm LBFGS
tuning default
template eon-svn/lj38-noise-1e-2
problem minimization/lj38-noise
reducer harness
cap 10000
n 1000
par2_mean 1906.855
nfailed 88
mean_calls 160.394
median_calls 153.0
min_calls 68.0
max_calls 402.0
n_crash 0
n_divergence 0
n_cap 0
n_wrong_stationary 88
n_replicates 2
n_differing 0
success_rate 0.912
wilson_low 0.8928277489502235
wilson_high 0.9280190020576792
